## CONFIGURING STATIC IP
- This is crucial because we need to ensure the server always has the same IP addresss. By default, Windows uses DHCP, which can assign a different IP after a reboot. 
- A Domain Controller must always be reachable at the same address because every client computer depends on it. This matters as well to keep DNS records accurate and Active Directory services to stay reliable.

Key Commands: ipconfig - reveals the basic ipv4 address, subnet mask, and default gateway, ping- verifies network conectivity by sending data packets, helping diagnose whter a device is reachable and checks your connection's latency

